{"id":"ASE-65","uuid":"723182f2-bea3-456a-acd8-7447d02e57fe","title":"List split, title unit, and a sandbox reply carrying declared and flattened units","description":"In the same sandbox call, after the recipe returns, the runtime splits every list unit whose element holds a `<pre>`, `<img>`, `<figure>`, `<picture>` or `<svg>` at any depth into list part / code or image unit / list part, converts each part with the same converter (the part after continues `start` and opens with empty items at each enclosing level; an item that held only the block is not repeated), and prepends a `# <title>` unit when the extracted title is not empty. The reply carries the title, the declared units with their paths, and the flattened units. The host validates the declared units and returns the flattened units only when validation is clean.

